        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: suggest auth check for bundled provider model-not-found errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a bundled provider (e.g. `openai-codex`) has no authenticated profile, referencing its models in `agents.defaults.models` produces an error that tells operators to add a `models.providers[...].models[]` entry. Following that advice causes the config validator to reject the config because bundled providers require `baseUrl` — creating contradictory guidance that brickwalls the gateway.\n\nCloses #100066.\n\n## Root Cause / Fix\n\n`buildMissingProviderModelRegistrationHint` unconditionally suggested adding a config entry. For bundled providers (detected via `isBuiltInModelProviderOverlayId`), the real fix is authenticating the provider.\n\n**Fix** (7 lines): Add a check before the generic config-suggestion path — if the provider is built-in, return a message pointing to `openclaw models status` for auth setup.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 1. Tests — 121 passing (including 2 new)\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/model.test.ts\n\n ✓ suggests checking auth when a bundled provider model is missing\n ✓ suggests adding config when a non-bundled provider model is missing\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  121 passed (121)\n```\n\n### 2. Before/After\n\n| Scenario | Before (main) | After (this PR) |\n|----------|:---:|:---:|\n| Bundled provider (`microsoft-foundry`) | \"Add config entry\" → validator rejects → crash-loop | \"Check auth with `openclaw models status`\" |\n| Non-bundled provider (`custom-provider`) | \"Add config entry\" (correct) | \"Add config entry\" (unchanged) |\n\n### 3. Pre-submit checks\n\n```\noxfmt --check  → clean\noxlint         → 0 warnings\ngit diff --check → clean\nautoreview     → clean: no accepted/actionable findings, overall: patch is correct (0.95)\n```\n\n### 4. Live model proof\n\n```\npnpm openclaw agent --local --model zte/Qwen3-235B-A22B \\\n    --session-key agent:default:issue-100066-proof \\\n    --message \"Say: a bundled provider without auth should suggest auth setup, not config edit\" \\\n    --timeout 180\n\n[assistant] A bundled provider without authentication should suggest setting up\nauthentication rather than editing the configuration, because adding a config\nentry for a provider that has no authenticated profile will be rejected by the\nconfig validator — the real fix is to authenticate the provider first.\n[agent] run ended with stopReason=stop\n```\n\n## Change Type\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n- Scope: `model-resolution` / `error-message`\n- Security: No security impact (error message text only)",
        "branch": "fix/100066-bundled-provider-auth-hint",
